+## 🩺 Troubleshooting
+
+**Stuck at 5% "Connecting to Chrome DevTools tabs..."**
+Chrome 128+ silently drops DevTools sockets that it does not allowlist, and some clients get
+rejected because of the `permessage-deflate` WebSocket extension. The app now disables that
+extension, adds `--remote-allow-origins=*` when it launches Chrome, and puts a timeout on every
+DevTools command — a dead connection now fails with a clear message instead of hanging forever.
+If you start Chrome by hand, use:
+
+```powershell
+chrome.exe --remote-debugging-port=9222 --remote-allow-origins=* --user-data-dir="%LOCALAPPDATA%\ChromeCDPProfile"
+```
+
+**Nothing is logged / "Task Completed" with zeros**
+The sheet could not be read. Chrome must be signed into the Google account that owns the sheet.
+The run now logs which read strategy worked (CSV export, gviz CSV, or clipboard copy) and refuses
+to report success when no rows were found.
+
+**Prospect not found in Messenger**
+Use `https://www.facebook.com/messages/` and leave the conversation list visible. Rows whose
+thread could not be read are left untouched and listed as "needs review" instead of being held or deleted.
+
+**How the DM check works**
+The run first reads and scrolls your whole Messenger conversation list (pausing ~3.5s after each
+scroll so the next batch loads) and indexes every thread it sees. Each prospect is looked up in
+that index and the matching thread is opened and read; Messenger search is only used when the
+scan cannot see them. If the list cannot be scanned at all, unverified rows are reported as
+"needs review" rather than assumed to be un-DM'd.
+
 ## 📋 Technical Playbook Rules Followed
 - **Messenger is the source of truth.**
 - Follower count rules applied for lead prioritization.
-- Safety checks before cell writing and row deletion.
+- Safety checks before every cell write, plus a read-back verification of both sheets.
 - Automated clipboard write: `Set-Clipboard -Value "done"`.
